{"id": "hiring-001", "category": "appointment_hiring", "question": "What are the main hiring steps from candidate sourcing to final employment offer at UoS?", "expected_route": "list", "expected_pages": [59, 60, 61], "expected_answer": "Candidate sourcing, structured candidate assessment and interview process, central committee review, initiating the employment process, and candidate communication and offer (sections 2.2.3.3 to 2.2.3.7).", "grading": "must_include", "must_include": [["sourcing", "source"], ["interview", "assessment"], ["central committee", "committee"], ["offer"]], "must_not_include": [], "source": "part1_pilot", "part1_verdict": "partial", "part1_ref": "Report Table 6-2, pilot Q9 (score 3/5)", "evidence_quote": "2.2.3.3 Candidate Sourcing; 2.2.3.4 Structured Candidate Assessment and Interview Process; 2.2.3.5 Central Committee Review; 2.2.3.6 Initiating the Employment Process; 2.2.3.7 Candidate Communication and Offer", "notes": "Multi-step procedure. Part 1 note: 'incomplete compared with the full recruitment process' - a bug 2 case. Route expectation is 'list': the question asks for an ordered set of steps, which is an enumeration."}
{"id": "calendar-004", "category": "date", "question": "What are the most important Fall 2025/2026 dates faculty should know?", "expected_route": "date", "expected_pages": [49], "expected_answer": "Return of academic staff 18 Aug; classes begin 25 Aug; last day for Add/Drop 28 Aug; midterms 13-23 Oct; classes end 04 Dec; final exams 06-16 Dec.", "grading": "must_include", "must_include": [["25 aug", "25 august", "august 25"], ["dec", "december"]], "must_not_include": ["2024/2025"], "source": "part1_pilot", "part1_verdict": "incorrect", "part1_ref": "Report Table 6-2, pilot Q10 (score 1/5)", "evidence_quote": "Mon 25 Aug Classes begin; Thu 28 Aug Last day for Add/Drop; Thu 04 Dec Classes end; Sat-Tue 06-16 Dec Final Exams", "notes": "Part 1 note: 'returned only one date and the wrong academic year'. The wrong year is a TYPO IN THE HANDBOOK: the first row of the Fall 2025/2026 table on page 49 reads 'Beginning of regular online admission in Fall 2024/2025'. '2024/2025' is banned so the harness detects the model repeating that row as the answer."}
{"id": "aipolicy-001", "category": "ai_policy", "question": "What does the handbook say about responsible AI use, academic integrity, and verifying AI-generated content?", "expected_route": "policy", "expected_pages": [269, 270], "expected_answer": "AI use must be ethical and responsible, AI may produce incorrect or misleading results, the University's Code of Academic Integrity remains paramount, responsibility for submitted work lies with the submitter, and attribution and citation must be accurate.", "grading": "must_include", "must_include": [["ethical", "responsible"], ["academic integrity"], ["incorrect", "misleading", "inaccurate", "hallucination", "verify"]], "must_not_include": [], "source": "part1_pilot", "part1_verdict": "correct", "part1_ref": "Report Table 6-2, pilot Q11 (score 4/5)", "evidence_quote": "AI technology is a permanent feature in the academic landscape, and its use must be ethical and responsible... AI technology is still evolving and may produce incorrect or misleading results. The University's Code of Academic Integrity remains paramount", "notes": "Three sub-questions in one query."}
{"id": "research-001", "category": "research_grants_tto", "question": "What support does UoS provide for conference participation, research grants, and technology transfer?", "expected_route": "policy", "expected_pages": [154, 155], "expected_answer": "Internal funding includes Seed, Competitive, Targeted and Collaborative Research Grants plus conference participation grants; the Technology Transfer Office manages intellectual property and licensing.", "grading": "must_include", "must_include": [["conference"], ["seed", "competitive", "targeted", "collaborative"], ["technology transfer", "tto"]], "must_not_include": [], "source": "part1_pilot", "part1_verdict": "partial", "part1_ref": "Report Table 6-2, pilot Q12 (score 3/5)", "evidence_quote": "1. Seed Research Grant... 2. Competitive Research Grant... 3. Targeted Research Grant... 4. Collaborative Research Grant... extra conference participation grants... 8.2.3 Technology Transfer Office", "notes": "Three sub-questions spanning two pages. Part 1 note: 'omitted important grant categories'."}
{"id": "workload-001", "category": "workload", "question": "How does the Workload Allocation Model work, and what teaching-load reductions are available?", "expected_route": "policy", "expected_pages": [89, 90], "expected_answer": "The Workload Allocation Model derives from Articles 20 and 21 of University President Decision No. (3) of 2019 and defines faculty workload in credit hours and contact hours for full-time faculty and academic non-faculty. One documented reduction is 6 credit hours in the first year for faculty on the Assistant Professor Emirati Track (page 65).", "grading": "must_include", "must_include": [["workload", "wlam"], ["credit hour", "contact hour"], ["reduction", "reduced"]], "must_not_include": [], "source": "part1_pilot", "part1_verdict": "partial", "part1_ref": "Report Table 6-2, pilot Q13 (score 3/5)", "evidence_quote": "3.11 Workload Allocation Model (WLAM) - Articles 20 and 21 of the University President Decision No. (3) of 2019... 2.9.1.3 Teaching Load Reduction: In the first year of appointment, faculty on the Assistant Professor Emirati Track are entitled to a teaching load reduction of 6 credit hours.", "notes": "The two halves of this question live on pages 89-90 and page 65. Answering both requires evidence from non-adjacent pages, so it is a retrieval-spread test as well as a multi-part test."}
{"id": "evaluation-003", "category": "evaluation", "question": "How is faculty performance evaluated, what are the rating categories, and what must be updated in FIS?", "expected_route": "", "expected_pages": [128], "expected_answer": "All performance evaluations are conducted through the Faculty Information System. The overall rating categories are Excellent (90-100), Very Good (80-89), Meets Expectation (70-79) and Needs Attention (0-69). Faculty must keep their profile updated and ensure research activities, teaching schedule, workload, end-of-course evaluations and peer observation display correctly.", "grading": "must_include", "must_include": ["excellent", "very good", ["meets expectation", "meets expectations"], "needs attention", "profile"], "must_not_include": [], "source": "part1_pilot", "part1_verdict": "partial", "part1_ref": "Report Table 6-2, pilot Q14 (score 3/5)", "evidence_quote": "Excellent 90-100; Very Good 80-89; Meets Expectation 70-79; Needs Attention 0-69. 6.9 The Faculty Information System - All performance evaluations are conducted through the Faculty Information System", "notes": "Three sub-questions, all supported by page 128. Part 1 note: 'the FIS portion was better than the rating-categories portion'. The single clearest bug 2 case in the whole set. Route is deliberately NOT scored for this case. The question carries three different intents (procedure, list, procedure) and no single label is defensible, so scoring one would measure the rubric rather than the classifier. This is the case that query decomposition would fix."}
{"id": "research-002", "category": "research_grants_tto", "question": "What are the core ethical principles that guide research at UoS?", "expected_route": "list", "expected_pages": [161], "expected_answer": "Integrity; Respect for Persons; Beneficence and Non-maleficence; Justice.", "grading": "must_include", "must_include": ["integrity", "respect for persons", ["beneficence", "non-maleficence"], "justice"], "must_not_include": [], "source": "part1_pilot", "part1_verdict": "correct", "part1_ref": "Report Table 6-2, pilot Q15 (score 5/5)", "evidence_quote": "Research conducted under the auspices of the University of Sharjah shall be guided by the following core ethical principles: Integrity... Respect for Persons... Beneficence and Non-maleficence... Justice", "notes": "Four-item list that Part 1 answered correctly. A regression guard for the bug 2 prompt change."}
{"id": "aipolicy-002", "category": "ai_policy", "question": "What does the handbook say about the ethical use of AI and large language models for faculty and students?", "expected_route": "policy", "expected_pages": [268, 269, 270], "expected_answer": "Section 16.6 gives University guidelines on AI and LLMs: use must be ethical and responsible, AI should enhance rather than hinder human creativity, AI may produce incorrect results, the Code of Academic Integrity remains paramount, and separate guidelines are given for students and for faculty.", "grading": "must_include", "must_include": [["ethical", "responsible"], ["academic integrity", "integrity"]], "must_not_include": [], "source": "part1_pilot", "part1_verdict": "correct", "part1_ref": "Report Table 6-2, pilot Q16 (score 4/5)", "evidence_quote": "16.6 University of Sharjah Guidelines on Artificial Intelligence and Large Language Models... its use must be ethical and responsible... The University's Code of Academic Integrity remains paramount", "notes": ""}
{"id": "research-003", "category": "research_grants_tto", "question": "What is the role of the Technology Transfer Office at UoS?", "expected_route": "policy", "expected_pages": [155], "expected_answer": "The Technology Transfer Office manages all intellectual property matters related to research at UoS, governs ownership and commercial development of inventions and creative works, safeguards the IP rights of faculty, staff and students, and facilitates licensing to external parties.", "grading": "must_include", "must_include": ["intellectual property", ["licensing", "commercial", "license"]], "must_not_include": [], "source": "part1_pilot", "part1_verdict": "correct", "part1_ref": "Report Table 6-2, pilot Q17 (score 5/5)", "evidence_quote": "The Technology Transfer Office (TTO) is entrusted with managing all intellectual property matters related to research activities and outputs at UoS... safeguards the intellectual property rights of faculty, staff, and students, and facilitates licensing to external parties.", "notes": "TTO is also described on page 175. Both pages are acceptable evidence, but page 155 is the definition section."}
{"id": "research-004", "category": "research_grants_tto", "question": "What kinds of research grants does UoS support for faculty research projects?", "expected_route": "policy", "expected_pages": [154, 155], "expected_answer": "Seed Research Grant, Competitive Research Grant, Targeted Research Grant and Collaborative Research Grant, plus research visits grants, summer stay research grants, extra conference participation grants, researcher hosting grants, exchange student researcher grants and graduate research assistant grants.", "grading": "must_include", "must_include": ["seed", "competitive", "targeted", "collaborative"], "must_not_include": [], "source": "part1_pilot", "part1_verdict": "correct", "part1_ref": "Report Table 6-2, pilot Q18 (score 5/5)", "evidence_quote": "1. Seed Research Grant... 2. Competitive Research Grant... 3. Targeted Research Grant... 4. Collaborative Research Grant", "notes": "Four-item list spanning a page break (pages 154 and 155). Tests whether chunking keeps the list together."}
